{"id": 78, "ts": 1780608525.1908267, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I acknowledge Emily\u2019s point that Candidate\u202fA lacks any documented evidence of staying calm under pressure, which is indeed a critical gap. However, I remain convinced that A\u2019s combination of anticipating dangerous situations, seeing complex connections, and excellent spatial vision directly supports the core safety and navigation demands of long\u2011haul flights. These technical strengths, together with his very good leadership qualities, suggest he would be able to make high\u2011quality decisions even in complex scenarios\u2014an inference supported by the fact that he can anticipate danger. While his show\u2011off demeanor and resistance to new ideas are concerns for crew cooperation, they are not yet proven to impair safety\u2011critical performance. Given that Candidate\u202fB, despite strong stress handling, has a documented pattern of making nasty remarks that could erode crew trust, I still vote for Candidate\u202fA as the best overall fit."}
